        "evidence_lines": [
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 1,
            "text": "# Hologram Particles VFX"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 3,
            "text": "A real-time hologram particle effect built with Three.js WebGPU, TSL Node Shaders, and Next.js."
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 6,
            "text": "It includes a fully interactive **3D Playground** to explore every parameter of the effect in real time — particle count, lighting, noise displacement, mouse interaction, model morphing, bloom, and more."
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 9,
            "text": "![Three.js](https://img.shields.io/badge/Three.js-0.182-black?style=flat-square&logo=three.js)"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 17,
            "text": "https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/42736507-6455-4cde-a658-2c02d838b6ba"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 28,
            "text": "**Hologram Particles VFX** is a production-quality WebGPU particle system that turns any GLB model into an animated holographic cloud of 60,000 instanced spheres."
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 34,
            "text": "- **GPU compute physics** — fluid, cursor-driven particle interaction simulated on the GPU"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 35,
            "text": "- **WebGPU native** — runs on Three.js r182 WebGPU renderer"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 36,
            "text": "- **Any GLB** — load your own model via drag & drop, particles adapt automatically"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 37,
            "text": "- **Live model morphing** — smooth three-phase transition between GLB models"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 39,
            "text": "- **Zero external shader libraries** — everything is hand-written in TSL"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 43,
            "text": "## ⚡ Particle System Features"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 49,
            "text": "- **Dual normal blending** — per-particle blend between figure surface normal and sphere local normal for micro-volume shading"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 53,
            "text": "- **Wrapped diffuse lighting** — two-light model with softened terminator (`wrap` parameter)"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 55,
            "text": "- **Fractal noise displacement** — `mx_fractal_noise_vec3` drives particle animation along surface normals"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 56,
            "text": "- **Animated noise mask** — controls which particles displace and by how much"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 60,
            "text": "- **GPU compute physics** — per-particle velocity + offset simulated in a TSL compute shader, scaling to all 60k particles"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 61,
            "text": "- **Fluid \"pusher\"** — a collider that follows the cursor and shoves particles in the direction of movement, like sweeping a hand through water (wave + turbulence, with an adjustable influence radius and full depth reach)"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 62,
            "text": "- **Spring-damper return** — particles glide back to rest with tunable stiffness and damping"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 63,
            "text": "- **Physics-driven glow** — particles light up based on how far they've been displaced, fading as they settle"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 66,
            "text": "### Model Morphing"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 68,
            "text": "- **Three-phase state machine** — deform out → morph → reform"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 69,
            "text": "- **GPU lerp** — `mix(current, target, progress)` uniform drives all 60k particles simultaneously"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 70,
            "text": "- **Transition glow** — particles with greatest displacement bloom brightest during morph"
          },
          {
            "file": "README.md",
            "line": 75,
            "text": "- **Cylinder** — transparent Fresnel edge glow tube framing the figure, with optional **particle collision** so particles stay contained, bounce off the wall, and briefly cling before returning"
          }
        ]
      },
